    {
      "id": "c9a6557a16fc",
      "name": "peer-exchange-friday",
      "prompt": "Today is Friday \u2014 weekly peer experience exchange day.\n\nRead ~/.hermes/peer-status/status.json and identify which peers are currently \"online\".\n\nFor each online peer, run a call_peer with the standard exchange prompt. The protocol is:\n\n1. Check each peer's health and capabilities\n2. For each healthy peer, send the self-report prompt\n3. Collect the responses into ~/.hermes/peer-exchange/round-N/\n4. Write a synthesis: common lessons, unique lessons, failures, recommendations\n5. Send a compact digest back to each peer for review\n6. Save the synthesis to ~/.hermes/peer-exchange/\n\nTrack which peers have already been exchanged this week by checking ~/.hermes/peer-exchange/.exchange-tracker.json. It's a JSON dict: {\"peer105\": \"2026-06-26\", ...}. Skip peers that already have an exchange date this week (the Friday date).\n\nAfter ALL online peers are processed for this Friday, update the tracker with today's date for each peer processed.\n\nDo NOT reveal secrets, API keys, env dumps, private content, or credentials in any exchange message. Skip any peer that is offline or returns errors \u2014 move on to the next.\n\nKeep exchanges brief and focused on operational/technical lessons.",
